%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 07cad028436a1b84eaed97906ca20508, type: 3}
  m_Name: DepthEvents
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  events:
  - Name: Intro
    EventID: R1
    Text: "Hello? Hello hello? You there, Newbie?| Okay, well, if you can hear me,
      that means you were able to figure out the Radio. Good news, good news. If
      you can\u2019t hear me, too bad. I don\u2019t really got all day to wait around
      and watch ya press buttons till you find the right frequency, yanno?| Uh, let\u2019s
      see here\u2026| Huh, that\u2019s new. Gettin\u2019 some funky echo through
      the speaker\u2026 must be \u2018cause it\u2019s old.| Uhh, yeah\u2026 Terminal\u2026
      transmitter\u2026 yeah. Yeah, yeah, this is\u2014 this is too much too fast
      for a newbie like you.| How \u2018bout this for now: I\u2019m Keith, The Halley
      Company\u2019s resident Radio Operator. I\u2019ll be broadcasting, um, every
      once in a while to help ya out in your diving bell, so don\u2019t forget this
      frequency, you hear?| Okay, what else\u2026 oh, right, right. Just so you know,
      I can\u2019t actually see inside the Bell. So you\u2019ve got sooome privacy,
      just, uh\u2026 don\u2019t do anything weird, \u2018kay? You don\u2019t wanna
      go down as that guy.| Anyways, should be a panel of Switches somewhere. Flip
      \u2018em all on, and, uh, the Bell\u2019ll start to descend.| I\u2019ll let
      you go, then\u2014 it\u2019s gonna take a sec to get your bearings once things
      start movin\u2019. Trust me.| Talk to you soon-ish. And, uh, congrats on becoming
      Operator."
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 04d6a076b23db484daf728ba390c1f7b, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 0
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 040000000d0000000300000006000000090000000c0000000d000000060000000600000004000000
  - Name: Post-Intro Bark
    EventID: T1
    Text: I know you're just going straight down, but in the perpetual darkness,
      I'd never find my way. Kudos to you, really.
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 200
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: Gauges
    EventID: E1
    Text: "Hello? Ya there, Op? Hope you don\u2019t mind a good ol\u2019 nickname.|
      Me again. Forgot to mention somethin\u2019. Whoops.| Uhh, the Bell might look
      a bit different from what you saw during the briefing\u2014 this is an older
      model from a few years back. It doesn\u2019t have all the fancy new features,
      so you\u2019re gonna hafta maintain this guy for, uh\u2026 uh, your entire
      expedition.| Gives ya somethin\u2019 to do while you\u2019re plungin\u2019
      into the \u201Cdeep wonders of below,\u201D as The Halley Company likes to
      say, you know?| But yeah. Should be a Gauge somewhere\u2014 you might not hear
      any steam releasing yet, uh, but if you do, that\u2019s no good, no good at
      all.| Hold the lever on the pipe down, and, uh, that\u2019ll gradually normalize
      the pressure in there. You\u2019ll know it worked if the red light turns off.
      Oh, and, uh, don\u2019t overdo it\u2014 make sure to keep the indicator in
      the middle range, got it got it?| It was a huge pain in the ass to get the
      last Bell up when the Operator didn\u2019t maintain it, so let\u2019s just
      stay on top of that for everyone\u2019s sake, okay?| Good luck, buddy."
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 25b35b0a139aa3b42b5a9107897ab7ab, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 600
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: -50
    TextTiming: 05000000040000000e00000006000000090000000b0000000800000002000000
  - Name: Fearmongering
    EventID: R2
    Text: "Salutations, Op. Man, coming up with these greetings is tough.| How\u2019s
      maintenance goin\u2019? Got a handle on it yet?| I\u2019d hope so, y\u2019know\u2014
      submersible catastrophes are noooot pretty. Lots of, uh, projectile dismemberment.
      No one wants to see that.| And, well, you can\u2019t really do anything about
      this part, but thousands of meters down? Water gets heaaavy. Combine that with
      poor manufacturing, and ya just might hear one hell of a hull crunch, and then\u2026|
      Boom. Implosion.| Haha, I\u2019ll\u2014 I\u2019ll stop before I scare ya for
      real. Being isolated down there seems spooky enough as is. I\u2019ve noticed
      it\u2019s not uncommon to start hearing strange, strange voices in your head,
      and seeing all sorts of funky stuff, so\u2026 makes sense why astronauts have
      to go through so much training.| Anyways, I\u2019ve kept ya long enough. Just
      figured you\u2019d \u2018ppreciate the company. If you get bored, feel free
      ta check out the other Radio channels, ya hear?"
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 15aea8e097f57254b98f834118293114, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 2200
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 0500000003000000080000000c000000020000000f00000008000000
  - Name: Switches
    EventID: E2
    Text: "Hello? Yoohoo, Newbie.| Just Keith, checkin\u2019 in. Aren\u2019t I nice.|
      So, anything new or unusual on your end?| Well, if I\u2019m gonna be honest\u2026
      uh, we\u2019re detecting some anomalous behaviour. Can you turn towards the
      Switchbox and make sure all the switches are flicked up?| Ah-he-hem. I\u2014
      I\u2019ve got, um, documentation here, you see. Says somethin\u2019 about the
      Switchbox going out of wack occasionally under troubleshooting?| Mmhm. That\u2014
      the red light, I mean\u2014 shouldn\u2019t be happening.| Not sure what\u2019s
      goin\u2019 on, but red lights are usually a warning to maintain the Bell\u2019s
      systems. So, keep an eye on it, would ya? Like I said, the Bell you\u2019re
      in is an older model, so it might keep happenin\u2019.| Ta-ta for now."
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e690f1f5bc8295f49b59960af7a04a59, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 4000
    EventTriggerOffset: 400
    CheckpointDepthOffset: -200
    TextTiming: 0300000004000000040000000800000009000000050000000b00000001000000
  - Name: Post-Switches Bark
    EventID: T2
    Text: Iron maidens are kind of bell-shaped, aren't they? Iron't ya glad yours
      isn't tryin' ta kill you?
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 5000
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: Inhaler
    EventID: E3
    Text: "Heyooo, Newbie. Ya feelin\u2019 crazy yet?| You\u2019re looking kinda
      rough. They want me to tell you that with the changes in pressure \u2018n stuff
      it\u2019s normal to be a bit dizzy.| Not that I\u2019m saying that you are\u2014
      but, uhh, if you are, there should be an Inhaler lying around. L-shaped, red,
      plastic? Whenever your vision starts getting fuzzy or you\u2019re having a
      hard time breathing, give that guy a goood drag, and the meds should fix ya
      right up.| What\u2019s in the meds? Couldn\u2019t tell ya, honestly. Heard
      they can feel pre\u2019tty good, though.| Puff puff, Op."
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 41f961de1cb132546ace95d4e36abfdf, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 6000
    EventTriggerOffset: 300
    CheckpointDepthOffset: -200
    TextTiming: 0500000006000000100000000700000001000000
  - Name: Pre-Chat Bark
    EventID: T3
    Text: "No offense, Op, but this is a snoozefest. What I wouldn't give for a vacation.
      Could use some cashmere hills filled with evergreens\u2026 but you've got the
      shortest end of the stick, so I can't complain."
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 7000
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: Chat Sesh
    EventID: R3
    Text: "Knock knock. Op, you there?| There\u2019s not actually all that much to
      do on this side, \u2018sides monitoring. None of the action you\u2019re getting.|
      So, uh, I\u2019ve got your file here\u2014 hope you don\u2019t mind me taking
      a peek. And, if you do\u2026 I already did. Sorry, sorry!| Mhm, mhm\u2026|
      Wow, you been with us ten years? Talk about dedication. Why the loyalty?| Uh,
      guess I can check for myself, here. Okay\u2026 vitals\u2026| Not bad, buddy.
      Rough neighbourhood, though.| NC connection code\u2026| Emergency contact\u2026|
      Oh, right. Uh, down the hallway, there should be a backup generator. I\u2019m
      meant to let ya know in case of emergencies.| Uhh, but, anyway, uh, reason
      for applying is that you heard successful Operators get a promotion? Really?|
      That can\u2019t be it. No dyin\u2019 family or anything? Says you got a dog\u2014
      your dog doing alright?| I hope you left her in good company.| Well, either
      way. Straightforward. I respect it.| Hm, risking it all for some extra cash,
      huh. So, how far would ya go? Would you sell your soul? Would you sell your
      mind?| Whoops, got a liiiil\u2019 too serious there. Just pullin\u2019 your
      leg\u2014 nothing to do with me in the end, right right?| Rootin\u2019 for
      you, Newbie."
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5fa79d751b2809349b5933cbe0bd99cc, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 7100
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 03000000040000000b00000003000000060000000500000004000000020000000300000008000000080000000800000003000000040000000a0000000700000002000000
  - Name: Post-Chat Sesh Bark
    EventID: T4
    Text: How much do you think a mind weighs?
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 9800
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: Blackout
    EventID: E4
    Text: "Newbie? Hey, Newbie? I know you\u2019re there\u2014 can ya hear me?| So,
      how badly did you want that promotion, again? Just so you know, that\u2019s
      not happening anymore.| You\u2019re pretty upset, aren\u2018tcha?| That\u2019s
      okay\u2014 numbers tend to go up with big reactions.| As for why\u2026 hmm.|
      That health screening you had to do last month? That wasn\u2019t just a screening.
      They had to, ahem, \u201Creallocate funds\u201D to cover the cost of the mandatory
      procedure they did on ya. Installation\u2019s pricey these days!| Sorry to
      Stella, though.| That is your dog, right?| Hey, hey, remember, uh, what I was
      sayin\u2019 earlier about implosion? What if there\u2019s, like, a crack in
      the bell or somethin\u2019? You\u2019d expire, and then she would, too. Bet
      that makes the promotion feel a hell of a lot less important.| Or\u2014 what
      if there\u2019s a sea monster circling the diving bell? Ooh, what if you\u2019re
      actually a rat in a maze, and a scientist\u2019s recording your reactions?|
      What do you think those sounds are, Op?| Bit of unsolicited advice? Write Stella
      a letter. It\u2019ll last lon\u2014"
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5c3a2219eb68ce44fadad25c6105e897, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 11000
    EventTriggerOffset: 1385
    CheckpointDepthOffset: -200
    TextTiming: 0a000000090000000300000004000000020000001100000003000000030000000f0000000a0000000400000004000000
  - Name: Blackout Safe
    EventID: E5
    Text: 
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 12100
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: HallucinationMax Bark 1
    EventID: T5
    Text: How'd it feel to be trapped in an iron lung? Suffocating? Claustrophobic?
      Glad I'm not confined to one for the rest of my life, haha.
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 12400
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: His Voice
    EventID: R4
    Text: "Been a sec, Newbie.| Or\u2014 I guess you\u2019re experienced now, huh?
      I\u2019ll stick with Op.|  Look, bottom line is, you\u2019re not making it
      outta here. We\u2019ve been watching this whole time and, well, you\u2019ve
      been doing a great job \u2018n all, but your time\u2019s almost up.| Y\u2019know,
      in all my years as the Radio Guy, I\u2019ve never stepped foot into the Bell.
      Too many ghosts.| Spend enough time in there, and, uh, you\u2019ll start ta
      feel \u2018em\u2026| Or so I\u2019ve observed.| Or maybe what you\u2019re feeling
      is just\u2026| Our eyes on you? (Our eyes on you?)| Say, when\u2014 when you
      first booted up the Terminal, the sight was a little too familiar, wasn\u2019t
      it? Almost like something had crawled into your head and was, uh, transmitting
      your, mm, vision data.| Honestly, that wasn\u2019t supposed to happen\u2014
      but it worked out in the end, so.| For us, anyways.| You shoulda figured it
      out sooner, you really shoulda. It\u2019s too late no\u2014 well, it was always
      too late for you.| Goodbye, Op.| (Good bye, Op.)| (Good bye, Op.)| (Good bye,
      Op.)| (Good bye, Op.)| (Good bye, Op.)| (Good bye, Op.) "
    Audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a417339bab4f38942916bc0e96aecd20, type: 3}
    MessageTrigger: 12800
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 04000000070000000d00000008000000040000000400000004000000050000000f00000006000000030000000a00000001000000010000000100000001000000010000000100000001000000
  - Name: HallucinationMax Bark 2
    EventID: T6
    Text: What would you do if none of your experiences were actually yours alone?
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 14300
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
    TextTiming: 
  - Name: HallucinationMax Bark 3
    EventID: T7
    Text: '''pparently, explorers have barely seen the seafloor ''cause it''s mostly
      deep ocean. Think the observer effect plays a role? Maybe the creatures know
      we''re watching.'
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    MessageTrigger: 14700
    EventTriggerOffset: 0
    CheckpointDepthOffset: 0
